## Independent Source Inventory

Each original has two separate rectangular coordinate frames. They are not
subparts sharing one coordinate plane. Each frame has 18 half-unit columns and
12 half-unit rows, with the vertical axis at column 9 and the horizontal axis at
row 6. Counting uses frame limits and the exposed regular lattice; strokes
concealed by dense source hatching are not claimed individually visible.
The modern figures retain all four grids and separate frames.

Within each frame the normalized local extent is x from -4.5 to 4.5 and y from
-3 to 3. These extents describe the lattice/window, not a newly imposed finite
solution domain. The spec's panel translations are (0,+4) for (a) and (0,-4.5)
for (b). Subtracting these translations recovers the source-relative coordinates
in the tables below. Equal horizontal and vertical unit sizes are preserved.

### Figure 26(a)

The source has a shallow ascending solid separator through the origin, with
upper/upper-left hatching. At four half-cells left and two rows down from the
origin it crosses the local point (-2,-1); the opposite node is (2,1).
Short horizontal coordinate guides are distinguishable from the solid boundary.
The scale marks needed to interpret the line are available despite heavy hatch
interference. The unclear nearest negative x glyph is not transcribed.

| Mapped point | Local coordinate | Spec coordinate | In-group displacement |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `fig26-a-origin` | (0,0) | (0,4) | Endpoint of both origin-to-node relations |
| `fig26-a-node-c5-r8` | (-2,-1) | (-2,3) | `fig26-a-origin-to-left`: (-2,-1) |
| `fig26-a-node-c13-r4` | (2,1) | (2,5) | `fig26-a-origin-to-right`: (2,1) |

`fig26-a-three-source-nodes` covers their collinearity. The two invisible frame
clips have local coordinates (-4.5,-2.25) and (4.5,2.25), with corresponding
collinearity assertions. They are analytic window intersections, not printed
givens or marked line endpoints. The two horizontal-guide displacement
assertions cover their complete local intervals (-2,-1) to (0,-1) and (0,1)
to (2,1). The 18 x 12 grid assertion is `fig26-a-grid-18x12`.

In the final raster, the line remains solid and ascending, the two guide
heights agree with the scale, and the upper side alone is hatched. All frame
edges, axis arrowheads, axis names and labels fit. Hatch-clearance gaps around
labels do not form another set boundary. PASS.

### Figure 26(b)

The source has a steeper ascending solid separator, with the southeast/right-
below side hatched. The horizontal-axis crossing is one half-cell right of the
origin, (.5,0); the vertical-axis crossing is two rows below, (0,-1). The line
also passes through (1,1). The positive horizontal projection is retained.
The short negative projection is regularized in the modern figure; its extended
clean presentation is not claimed as an exact source ink fragment.

| Mapped point | Local coordinate | Spec coordinate | In-group displacement |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `fig26-b-origin` | (0,0) | (0,-4.5) | Endpoint of all three origin relations |
| `fig26-b-x-intercept-c10-r6` | (.5,0) | (.5,-4.5) | `fig26-b-origin-to-x-intercept`: (.5,0) |
| `fig26-b-y-intercept-c9-r8` | (0,-1) | (0,-5.5) | `fig26-b-origin-to-y-intercept`: (0,-1) |
| `fig26-b-unit-node-c11-r4` | (1,1) | (1,-3.5) | `fig26-b-origin-to-unit-node`: (1,1) |

`fig26-b-three-source-nodes` covers the three separator nodes. Invisible frame
clips are locally (-1,-3) and (2,3); both have collinearity assertions.
Guide displacement assertions cover (0,1) to (1,1) and (-1,-1) to (0,-1).
The 18 x 12 grid assertion is `fig26-b-grid-18x12`.

The final raster preserves the half-unit x crossing, negative y crossing, steep
slope, solid line and southeast hatch. The origin label is on the unhatched
side and the -1 mark is legible. The full lower frame is present. PASS.

### Figure 27(a)

The source circle is centered at the origin and reaches four half-cells in
each cardinal direction, a normalized radius of 2. Its vertical chord/cap
boundaries are two half-cells left and right of the origin, x=-1 and x=+1.
The two lateral caps alone are hatched; the middle strip and circle exterior
are not. Every chord terminates at its circle contacts, not at the grid edge.
The original glyphs used for positive scales are consistent with that lattice.
No unavailable negative glyph is reconstructed.

| Mapped point | Local coordinate | Spec coordinate | In-group displacement from origin |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `fig27-a-origin` | (0,0) | (0,4) | Endpoint of the following eight relations |
| `fig27-a-circle-left` | (-2,0) | (-2,4) | `fig27-a-origin-to-left-extreme`: (-2,0) |
| `fig27-a-circle-right` | (2,0) | (2,4) | `fig27-a-origin-to-right-extreme`: (2,0) |
| `fig27-a-circle-top` | (0,2) | (0,6) | `fig27-a-origin-to-top-extreme`: (0,2) |
| `fig27-a-circle-bottom` | (0,-2) | (0,2) | `fig27-a-origin-to-bottom-extreme`: (0,-2) |
| `fig27-a-left-chord-bottom` | (-1,-sqrt(3)) | (-1,2.2679491924) | `fig27-a-origin-to-left-bottom` |
| `fig27-a-left-chord-top` | (-1,+sqrt(3)) | (-1,5.7320508076) | `fig27-a-origin-to-left-top` |
| `fig27-a-right-chord-bottom` | (1,-sqrt(3)) | (1,2.2679491924) | `fig27-a-origin-to-right-bottom` |
| `fig27-a-right-chord-top` | (1,+sqrt(3)) | (1,5.7320508076) | `fig27-a-origin-to-right-top` |

All eight non-origin points have `pointOnCircle` assertions at radius 2.
`fig27-a-left-vertical-chord` and `fig27-a-right-vertical-chord` assert zero
horizontal displacement and a vertical span of 2*sqrt(3). The four contact
heights are modern analytic construction values, not source-printed numbers.
None is shown as an ordered pair or added question label.
The 18 x 12 grid assertion is `fig27-a-grid-18x12`.

#### H1 And Actual Raster Concern

The historical first H1 HOLD is not rewritten or replaced by this review.
I read the current targeted unresized-crop record at SHA-256
`1277ff87e6215d98ac79b8de54312b6ac24eece3a2c099e717e885c8fd5d5d15`,
but did not reopen its crop. That record supports a continuous source
upper-right arc only; it is neither whole-figure nor modern-output approval.
My own original-figure observation establishes the overall circle/cap structure.
The restricted H1 addendum supplies the finer historical arc-style adjudication.

The final 640 x 1024 raster visibly has pale grid crossings over the circular
stroke. Approximate full-raster locators include the shallow top near
(290..350,136..143), the corresponding bottom near (290..350,375..382), and
isolated grid crossings on the curved flanks. This concern is real, not dismissed
because the renderer reports pass or because the circle object is mathematically
correct.

At the authorized normal-width view, the circular rim remains traceable as a
solid outline: the pale interruptions coincide with the visible lattice, and
substantial dark arc runs join the same contour. They do not read as a deliberate
regular dashed boundary. All four chord contacts, the solid vertical cutoffs,
the radius and the inside/outside distinction remain clear. The cap hatching
neither leaks outside the circle nor fills the middle strip. I do not find an
instructional reason to change inclusion/line-style interpretation from these
local overlays. This is a nonblocking raster-quality observation, not a defect
requiring another repair. No exact pixel-connectivity or forensic rendering-
cause guarantee is claimed. PASS for the current raster.

### Figure 27(b)

The source junction is two half-unit rows above the origin, (0,1).
The x-axis crossings are two half-unit columns to either side, (-1,0) and
(1,0). The source contains two complete solid diagonal lines, including both
right-hand continuations. Only the left-facing wedge between them is hatched;
this is not merely a pair of left rays or an upper/lower wedge.

| Mapped point | Local coordinate | Spec coordinate | In-group displacement |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `fig27-b-origin` | (0,0) | (0,-4.5) | Endpoint of all three origin relations |
| `fig27-b-junction-c9-r4` | (0,1) | (0,-3.5) | `fig27-b-origin-to-junction`: (0,1) |
| `fig27-b-negative-crossing-c7-r6` | (-1,0) | (-1,-4.5) | `fig27-b-origin-to-negative-crossing`: (-1,0) |
| `fig27-b-positive-crossing-c11-r6` | (1,0) | (1,-4.5) | `fig27-b-origin-to-positive-crossing`: (1,0) |

The ascending line's local window clips are (-4,-3) and (2,3); the descending
line's are (-2,3) and (4,-3). Each of the four has its collinearity assertion
with the appropriate crossing and junction. These unlabelled analytic clips
do not assert source-printed endpoints. The grid assertion is
`fig27-b-grid-18x12`.

The final raster shows the correct junction, both x crossings, all four line
branches and the left wedge. The y=1 scale glyph remains readable despite its
nearby hatch-clearance opening. Full frame and axis arrows are visible. PASS.

## Read-Only Mathematical And Binding Checks

An independent read-only arithmetic/reference inspection of the parsed current
specs exited 0. It did not invoke a native validator, renderer or old PASS check.
All 17 fig-26 assertions and all 27 fig-27 assertions satisfy their declared
tolerances. This includes grid dimensions, displacements, collinearity and
circle membership. All inventory object/assertion IDs resolve.

Every mapped point is covered by a mapped multi-point relation wholly inside
its own `pointRelationships` inventory group: 3 + 4 points for fig-26, and
9 + 4 points for fig-27, totaling 20. Relationships to unmapped construction
points were not used as substitutes. All four source grid groups have their
own `gridDimensions` assertion.

The read-only check also inspected both endpoints of all 137 fig-26 hatch
segments and all 68 fig-27 hatch segments against their intended region and
the normalized frame. They remain inside their respective linear half-planes,
convex circular caps or wedge. Convexity makes endpoint containment sufficient
for each straight segment. Uniform pitch/orientation, tiny endpoint dots, label
clearance, the cleaned lower guide, English panel captions and vertical panel
relayout are modern presentational regularizations, not additional printed
source givens.

Both existing render reports have status `pass`, no reported collisions, and
one declared width check at 640 with minimum text 20 px against required
16 px. The PNG headers independently confirm 640 x 1024, matching the SVG
canvas and viewBox. Visible PNG labels are readable and fit the full canvas.
The SVGs contain semantic `--ld-figure-*` variables. Alternate themes were not
rendered or visually approved in this bounded task.

Each actual source/spec/render/SVG/PNG hash matches the author receipt, and
each render report binds its actual current spec and SVG. The input bytes were
checked before and after image observation. No renderer-output determinism or
author self-observation was substituted for source comparison.

